  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Atom <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> occupies FCC lattice sites as well as alternate tetrahedral voids of FCC. In FCC, tetrahedral voids are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> (in a unit cell) Hence</p><p>Atom <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> in a unit cell (FCC lattice sites)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Atom <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> in a unit cell (in T.V.) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Total atom<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> &nbsp;in one unit cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>For relation between a and r, since Tetrahedral void&nbsp;&nbsp;forms at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>th of body diagonal,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Packing efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
